# Snake run artifacts. scripts/snake.ps1 appends its report block to
# docs/plans/<slug>-report.md on every run. That is a log of what happened, not
# a record of what was authorised — the plan file is the record. Ignored so it
# cannot drift into a commit and be mistaken for one.
#
# NOTE (merge, 2026-09-21): docs/plans/env-local-report.md and
# docs/plans/operating-protocol-report.md are already TRACKED on this lineage, and
# .gitignore never untracks anything, so they stay. This rule governs new ones only.
docs/plans/*-report.md

# Credentials. The ignore rule exists BEFORE the file it protects, so there is no
# window in which a careless `git add -A` can stage a real token.
# .env.example IS committed — it is the documentation. .env.local never is.
#
# Order matters here: `.env.*` would swallow .env.example, so the negation follows it.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Terraform. tfvars and state both carry credentials in plain text.
*.tfvars
*.tfstate*
.terraform/
crash.log

# Private keys.
*.pem
id_ed25519*

# Build output.
*.log
out/
output/
bin/
obj/

# ...except a run order's transcript, which is EVIDENCE and is mandated by the plan that
# produced it. The `*.log` above would swallow docs/plans/<slug>/TRANSCRIPT.log, which
# HASHES.txt is computed over — making COMBINED unreproducible from a clone while every
# local check still passed. Recorded as F-31 in the compliance plan.
#
# This is a DELIBERATE ADDITION to the union, not a line either side carried: without it
# this pass cannot commit its own evidence. See FINDINGS.md FINDING-M7.
!docs/plans/**/TRANSCRIPT.log
